,guide_user_install_title:"Install apps",guide_user_install_1:"App Store (🛒): browse and install demo apps to the desktop.",guide_user_install_2:"Publish: drop a hosted .zip (manifest inside) or an iframe manifest.json — draft until DEV approves. Close all windows before drop.",guide_user_install_3:"Duplicate names: Replace, Keep both (numbered name), or Cancel.",guide_user_start_title:"Start menu",guide_user_start_1:"Click the Windows icon on the taskbar — search apps and open pinned apps.",guide_user_start_2:"Open Settings (⚙️) for screen and keyboard options.",guide_user_tips_title:"Tips",guide_user_tips_1:"File drop only works on the main desktop (no windows open).",guide_user_tips_2:"Built-in apps (App Store, Guide, Settings) cannot be renamed or removed.",guide_user_tips_3:"Building an app? Open App bridge for how to connect and use permissions.",guide_dev_who_title:"Who this is for",guide_dev_who_1:"You build an app that opens inside App Hub when a user clicks it on the desktop.",guide_dev_who_2:"App Hub gives you AppHubBridge — ask for permissions, show desktop messages, and read a safe UI snapshot of the signed-in user.",guide_dev_runtime_title:"Pick a runtime type",guide_dev_runtime_1:"hosted — ship a zip; Hub stores and serves your build. Best for small tools and demos.",guide_dev_runtime_2:"iframe — you host a SPA at entry_url (HTTPS). Best for full apps, auth, and your own domain storage.",guide_dev_runtime_3:"In manifest.json set runtime_type to hosted or iframe. Iframe also needs entry_url.",guide_dev_bridge_title:"Launch & bridge handshake",guide_dev_bridge_1:"1) User opens your app → Hub calls POST /apps/{slug}/launch (returns launch_token + expires_in + scopes_granted).",guide_dev_bridge_2:"2) Hub opens your runtime and sends apphub:bridge:ready (slug, launch_token, session_id, api bases, version, display_user). While the window stays open, Hub refreshes the short launch_token and re-sends ready — use the latest token if you cache it.",guide_dev_bridge_3:"3) Use window.AppHubBridge or listen for apphub:bridge:ready. Parent callParent before DEV approve may return demo fixtures (Demo badge); after approve + relaunch you get real parent.* scopes. Copy docs/sdk-stub.js if you need a ready-made client.",guide_dev_storage_title:"Storage (hosted zip only)",guide_dev_storage_1:"Hosted apps cannot use browser localStorage directly — Hub injects a shim for you.",guide_dev_storage_2:"Keep using localStorage in your code. Before the first read on load, await window.__APPHUB_STORAGE__?.ready.",guide_dev_storage_3:"Data is saved per Hub user and per app slug — other apps cannot read it. Iframe apps use normal storage on your entry_url origin.",guide_dev_permissions_title:"Permissions",guide_dev_permissions_1:"user.read — minimal id and display name.",guide_dev_permissions_2:"user.profile — extended profile (avatar, locale, etc.) when the user agrees.",guide_dev_permissions_3:"desktop.notify — POST bridge/notify from publisher backend (api_urls); desktop.message — Hub postMessage banner.",guide_dev_permissions_4:"desktop.badge — update your app button on the taskbar.",guide_dev_bridge_code_title:"Minimal example",guide_dev_bridge_code:`// After apphub:bridge:ready (hosted: await __APPHUB_STORAGE__?.ready first if using localStorage)
const bridge = window.AppHubBridge
const ctx = bridge.getContext() // app_slug, launch_token, publisher_api_base, app_version, …
const display = bridge.getDisplayUser() // UI only — not for auth
await bridge.requestPermission('desktop.message')
await bridge.sendDesktopMessage({
  type: 'banner',
  title: 'Hello',
  body: 'Welcome ' + (display?.name ?? ''),
  duration_ms: 5000
})
// Verified user: your backend calls GET …/bridge/user with launch_token`,guide_dev_user_title:"User info — two levels",guide_dev_user_1:"UI only: getDisplayUser() or display_user on bridge:ready — greetings and labels inside your app.",guide_dev_user_2:"Trusted: your publisher backend calls GET bridge/user with the launch_token (needs user.read on the token).",guide_dev_user_3:"Never use display_user for authorization. Always handle denied permissions gracefully.",guide_dev_desktop_title:"Messages to desktop",guide_dev_desktop_1:"sendDesktopMessage sends banners or hints on the Hub desktop work area.",guide_dev_desktop_2:"Notifications use POST bridge/notify from your publisher backend — not AppHubBridge.notify.",guide_dev_desktop_3:"setTaskbarBadge(count) updates your app on the taskbar when desktop.badge is granted.",guide_dev_deploy_title:"Publish to App Hub",guide_dev_deploy_1:"Hosted: build dist → zip with manifest.json (runtime_type: hosted) → drop on desktop → DEV approves → appears in store.",guide_dev_deploy_2:"Iframe: host your SPA → manifest with runtime_type: iframe and entry_url (HTTPS) → drop manifest or POST /apps/register → DEV approves.",guide_dev_deploy_3:"List permissions and api_urls in manifest.json. Bump version when you re-publish.",guide_dev_docs_title:"Machine-readable reference (AI & tools)",guide_dev_docs_1:"Need the full reference? Open it below — written for humans, always synced with the latest publisher contract.",guide_dev_docs_link:"Open full publisher reference",guide_dev_docs_2:"Covers runtime types, bridge, permissions, manifest, and how to publish.",guide_dev_docs_3:"Quick start is in the sections above; the full reference loads on demand.",guide_dev_docs_panel_title:"Full publisher reference",guide_dev_docs_close:"Close",guide_dev_docs_loading:"Loading publisher reference…",guide_dev_docs_ai_note_before:"AI coding tools use",guide_dev_docs_ai_note_after:"(JSON). That machine format is not shown here.",guide_dev_docs_error_no_ap